<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 September in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 11 September, from 1185 to 2001.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1185">1185 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">841 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Isaac II Angelos kills Stephen Hagiochristophorites and raises a revolt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When Stephen Hagiochristophorites, lieutenant of Emperor Andronikos I Komnenos, tried to arrest him, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-ii-angelos">Isaac II Angelos</a> killed him and took refuge in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>. His appeal to the people raised a revolt that deposed Andronikos and made Isaac emperor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac-ii-angelos">Isaac II Angelos</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1297">1297 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">729 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wallace and Moray defeat the English at Stirling Bridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Scottish forces under Andrew Moray and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a> destroyed an English army under the Earl of Surrey as it crossed the narrow bridge over the River Forth near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a>. Moray was severely wounded and died later that year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-stirling-bridge">Battle of Stirling Bridge</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1390 CE <span class="tih-ago">636 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Teutonic Knights and Vytautas begin a siege of Vilnius</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Lithuanian Civil War, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Knights</a> and their ally Vytautas began a five-week siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a>, whose castles were held by Skirgaila. The Knights ruined much of the outer city and destroyed the Crooked Castle but withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1697">1697 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">329 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prince Eugene of Savoy destroys the Ottoman army at Zenta</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy">Prince Eugene of Savoy</a> surprised the Ottoman army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mustafa II as it crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> at Zenta and destroyed it, killing tens of thousands, including the grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a>. The victory led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> of 1699.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-zenta">Battle of Zenta</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy">Prince Eugene of Savoy</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-turkish-war">Great Turkish War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1709">1709 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">317 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marlborough wins a costly victory at Malplaquet</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Marlborough and Prince Eugene drove a French army from its positions at Malplaquet, but lost far more men than the enemy. The bloodiest battle of the century strengthened calls in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> for peace.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1777">1777 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">249 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Howe defeats Washington at Brandywine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General William Howe outflanked Washington's army at Brandywine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>. Two weeks later the British occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>, and Congress fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1941">1941 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">85 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ground is broken for the Pentagon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Construction began on the Pentagon in Arlington, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, to house the War <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a>. Finished in just 16 months, it remains one of the world's largest office buildings.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Military coup overthrows Chile's President Allende</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Armed forces led by General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet">Augusto Pinochet</a> bombed the presidential palace, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende">Salvador Allende</a> died inside. The US had worked to undermine Allende; Pinochet's dictatorship killed and disappeared thousands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/al-qaeda" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-qaeda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2001">2001 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">25 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Al-Qaeda's September 11 attacks kill 2,977 people</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hijackers crashed airliners into the World Trade Center and the Pentagon; a fourth plane came down in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>. The attacks killed 2,977 people and led to the US-led wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
